  "description": "Introducing Kiyomori, this font presents a strong visual character inspired by classic Japanese aesthetics, particularly the spirit of samurai culture and traditional kanji calligraphy. Its letterforms are sharp and angular, with pointed terminals that resemble controlled brush strokes of sumi ink. The vertical structure feels disciplined and commanding, while the diagonal cuts and dramatic edges evoke the precision and energy of a katana blade. Each character blends gothic boldness with the expressive soul of Japanese calligraphic art.\nIn application, this font works exceptionally well for Japanese-themed designs, whether traditional or modern—such as streetwear branding, cultural posters, music titles, or visual projects. It delivers a bold, artistic, and distinctive presence, helping create a powerful visual identity. The combination of classic influence and contemporary edge makes this typeface dramatic yet highly relevant for modern design contexts.",
  "fullDescription": "<p>Introducing Kiyomori, this font presents a strong visual character inspired by classic Japanese aesthetics, particularly the spirit of samurai culture and traditional kanji calligraphy. Its letterforms are sharp and angular, with pointed terminals that resemble controlled brush strokes of sumi ink. The vertical structure feels disciplined and commanding, while the diagonal cuts and dramatic edges evoke the precision and energy of a katana blade. Each character blends gothic boldness with the expressive soul of Japanese calligraphic art.</p>\n<p>In application, this font works exceptionally well for Japanese-themed designs, whether traditional or modern—such as streetwear branding, cultural posters, music titles, or visual projects. It delivers a bold, artistic, and distinctive presence, helping create a powerful visual identity. The combination of classic influence and contemporary edge makes this typeface dramatic yet highly relevant for modern design contexts.</p>",
